messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe mobile phone usage of the administrative department of a company is as follows: 1. Xiao Wang dialed the phone of everyone in the administrative department; 2. Xiao Li once called Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao never called anyone else; 3. People who have never answered calls from others in the administration department have never called others.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings can be infered:\n# Options:\nA) Xiao zhao never answered a phone call from xiao li\nB) Xiao li once answered a phone call from xiao wang\nC) Someone in the administration department once called xiao wang\nD) Xiao wang answered the phone from everyone in the administration department', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and analyze each option step by step:.\n\n1.**Xiao Wang dialed the phone of everyone in the administrative department.**.\n   - This means Xiao Wang made calls to all members of the administrative department.\n\n2.**Xiao Li once called Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao never called anyone else.**.\n   - Xiao Li made a call to Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao did not make any calls to anyone else in the administrative department.\n\n3.**People who have never answered calls from others in the administration department have never called others.This does not imply that if someone has never received a call from another person, they have not made any calls to others.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:.\n\n**Option B: Xiao Zhao always answered a phone call from Xiao Li**.\n- From the information given, we cannot conclude that Xiao Li ever called Xiao Zhao, let alone that Xiao Zhao always answered the calls.Therefore, this statement is not supported by the information provided.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
