      "text": " A.\n3.**Option A**: The owner of the steel plant gave a gift of one million to the contractor in the neighboring county to better sell steel. This fits the definition of advertising as it is a commercial activity aimed at promoting the sale of steel through a gift, which is a form of promotion.\n4.**Option B**: In order to become president, Obama did not hesitate to make a speech on TV and newspapers. This is a political campaign, not a commercial one, and it is not aimed at promoting a specific product or service. Therefore, it does not fit the definition of advertising.\n5.**Option C**: The company stipulates that office computers must use a unified brand. This is a corporate policy to standardize the brand image, not a promotional activity aimed at selling a product or service. Therefore, it does not fit the definition of advertising.\n6.**Option D**: Li Ning brand clothing sponsored the French sports delegation to go to the Olympic Games, and obtained good social and economic benefits. This is a sponsorship, which is a form of advertising, but it is not a direct promotional activity aimed at selling the product. Therefore, it does not fit the definition of advertising as strictly as the other options.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct option is A.\n</think>\n<answer>A</answer>",
