 16%|#5        | 94/600 [03:36<04:22,  1.93it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe words we follow today to talk about ancient Chinese painting are all written by Chinese literati, and because of this, Chinese literati have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time, and they have become accustomed to starting from their own point of view. choose a point of view that is good for literati and artists, and now-- or should have been-- it's time for us to compete with them. And we should also question what they call a good painter or good work. Many excellent non-literati artists do not get due recognition because of the prejudice of literati. Here, we should give them objective evaluation and due status one by one.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements is consistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice\nC) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of chinese painting theory for a long time\nD) The difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has a long history", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s carefully analyze the context and the question.The context discusses the dominance of Chinese literati in the discussion and evaluation of ancient Chinese painting, their tendency to favor their own perspective, and the need for a more objective evaluation of non-literati artists.The question asks us to identify which statement is consistent with the original text.\n\nFirst, let\'s examine each option:.\n\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level.\n- The context does not provide any information about the appreciation level of literati artists compared to their creative level.It only mentions their dominance in the discussion and the need for a more objective evaluation of non-literati artists.Therefore, this statement is not supported by the context.\n\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice.\n- The context does not mention any specific instances of talented literati and artists being buried due to prejudice.It only talks about the need for a more objective evaluation of non-literati artists.Thus, this statement is not supported by the context.\n\nC) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of Chinese painting theory for a long time.\n- The context explicitly states that "Chinese literati have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time."This indirectly contradicts this statement.\n\nA) The similarity of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has a short history.\n- While the context mentions that the discussion and evaluation have been dominated by literati, it does not provide information about a short-lived similarity in interest between literati and non-literati painting.Therefore, this statement is not indirectly contradicted by the context.\n\nAfter analyzing each option, the statement that is inconsistent with the original text is:.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
