 18%|#8        | 110/600 [03:46<03:04,  2.66it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe wave of the world's high-tech revolution has pushed economic competition from material resource competition to human human resource competition. The development, utilization and management of human resources will become key factors in the development of human society and economy. In this process, a large amount of human resource information is needed. , Inevitably cannot do without human resource accounting. In our country with a large population and relatively poor population quality, it is more necessary to establish and implement a human resource accounting system.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options can be inferred from this text?\n# Options:\nA) The necessity of developing human resource accounting in china.\nB) The wave of high-tech revolution in the world has a great influence.\nC) The population of our country is large and the quality of the population is relatively poor.\nD) The competition of human resources has become the key factor of social development.", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - The context discusses the shift from material resource competition to human resource competition due to the high-tech revolution.\n   - It emphasizes the importance of human resource information and management in the development of human society and economy.\n   - The text highlights the need for a human resource accounting system in China, given its large population and relatively poor population quality.\n\n2.**Option A: The necessity of developing human resource accounting in China.**.\n   - The context explicitly mentions that "In our country with a large population and relatively poor population quality, it is more necessary to establish and implement a human resource accounting system.".\n   - This directly supports the necessity of developing human resource accounting in China.\n\n3.**Option B: The wave of high-tech revolution in the world has a great influence.**.\n   - While the context does mention the wave of the world\'s high-tech revolution, it does not explicitly state that it has a great influence.\n   - The influence is more implied rather than directly stated.\n\n4.**Option C: The population of our country is large and the quality of the population is relatively poor.**.\n   - The context does mention that the population of China is large and the quality of the population is relatively poor.\n   - However, this is a fact provided in the context and not a conclusion that can be inferred from it.The competition of human resources has not become the key factor of social development.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
