 36%|###5      | 215/600 [05:08<03:33,  1.80it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe 2010 Shanghai World Expo is an unprecedented event, with more than 200 national pavilions and enterprise theme pavilions. College student Wang Gang decided to visit the World Expo on the second day of his summer vacation. The night before last, he specially went online to check the netizens' suggestions on the selection of relevant popular venues. Among them, three attracted Wang Gang most: (1) if you visit the Saudi Arabia Pavilion, you won't visit the Oil Pavilion. (2) The Petroleum Museum and the China National Pavilion are optional. (3) Not both the China National Pavilion and the Petroleum Museum. In fact, Wang Gang had a very tight schedule for the World Expo the next day. He did not accept any of the above three suggestions.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is correct?\n# Options:\nA) Visit saudi arabia pavilion and petroleum pavilion, but not china national pavilion\nB) Saudi arabia pavilion, petroleum pavilion and china national pavilion were all visited\nC) Saudi arabia pavilion, petroleum pavilion and china national pavilion were not visited\nD) Did not visit saudi arabia pavilion, oil pavilion and china national pavilion", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given information and analyze each option step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - Wang Gang visited the World Expo on the second day of his summer vacation.\n   - He checked netizens\' suggestions for popular venues.\n   - Three suggestions stood out:.\n     1.If you visit the Saudi Arabia Pavilion, you won\'t visit the Oil Pavilion.\n     2.The Petroleum Museum and the China National Pavilion are optional.\n     3.Not both the China National Pavilion and the Petroleum Museum.\n   - Wang Gang did not accept any of these suggestions.\n\n2.**Option Analysis:**.\n   - **Option A:** Visit Saudi Arabia Pavilion and Petroleum Pavilion, but not China National Pavilion.\n     - This option directly contradicts the first suggestion: "If you visit the Saudi Arabia Pavilion, you won\'t visit the Oil Pavilion."Since the Oil Pavilion is the same as the Petroleum Pavilion, this option is invalid.\n   .\n   - **Option B:** Saudi Arabia Pavilion, Petroleum Pavilion, and China National Pavilion were all visited.This option directly supports the first suggestion: "If you visit the Saudi Arabia Pavilion, you won\'t visit the Oil Pavilion."Since the Oil Pavilion is the same as the Petroleum Pavilion, this option is valid.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
