 40%|####      | 241/600 [07:52<05:14,  1.14it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSmithtown University' s fund-raisers succeeded in getting donations from 80 percent of the potential donors they contacted. This success rate, exceptionally high for university fund-raisers, does not indicate that they were doing a good job. On the contrary, since the people most likely to donate are those who have donated in the past, good fund-raisers constantly try less-likely prospects in an effort to expand the donor base. The high success rate shows insufficient canvassing effort.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, provides more support for the argument?\n# Options:\nA) This year the average size of the donations to smithtown university from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before.\nB) The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for smithtown university this year were from donors who had never given to the university before.\nC) This year most of the donations that came to smithtown university from people who had previously donated to it were made without the university's fund-raisers having made any contact with the donors.\nD) Smithtown university's fund-raisers were successful in their contacts with potential donors who had never given before about as frequently as were fund-raisers for other universities in their contacts with such people.", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the question.The context states that the high success rate of 80 percent in getting donations from potential donors does not indicate that the fund-raisers are doing a good job.Instead, it suggests that the fund-raisers are not canvassing enough less-likely prospects to expand the donor base.The question asks which option provides more support for this argument.\n\nLet's evaluate each option:.\n\nA) This year the average size of the donations to smithtown university from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before.\n- This option talks about the average size of donations from new donors versus those who have donated before.It does not directly address the issue of canvassing effort or the effectiveness of the fund-raisers in reaching less-likely prospects.Therefore, it does not provide strong support for the argument.\n\nB) The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for smithtown university this year were from donors who had never given to the university before.\n- This option directly supports the argument.If the majority of the donations came from new donors, it implies that the fund-raisers were successfully reaching out to less-likely prospects, which contradicts the argument that the high success rate indicates insufficient canvassing effort.This option provides strong support for the argument.\n\nAfter evaluating all the options, neither option B nor C provide strong support for the argument.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
