messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBroken window effect is a psychological phenomenon, that is, if the window of a house is broken and no one repair it, and soon other windows will also be broken.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings does not belong to broken window effect?\n# Options:\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to understand the broken window effect and apply it to each of the given options.The broken window effect suggests that if a small problem (like a broken window) is not addressed, it will lead to more problems (like more broken windows).Let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n- This option describes a situation where a small problem (graffiti) is not addressed, leading to a larger problem (the wall being full of messy and ugly things).This fits the broken window effect.\n\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n- This option describes a situation where a small problem (rubbish in a clean place) is present, and it leads to a larger problem. Instead, it describes a behavior change where people do not feel ashamed to throw rubbish. This fits the broken window effect.\n\nA) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\n- This option describes a situation where a small problem (pollution in a tributary) is not addressed, leading to a larger problem (pollution in the whole basin). This does not fit the broken window effect.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
