 62%|######1   | 369/600 [11:33<02:24,  1.60it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNucleic acids and other genetic foods that appear in the name of health care products are not very helpful to human health. From a scientific point of view, the so-called human body needs to be supplemented with exogenous nucleic acids cannot be established. What the human body lacks is nutrition, and nucleic acid cannot be lacking. Some advertisements say that when people are old or sick, their ability to make genes will be weakened, which is even more nonsense.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options can be inferred?\n# Options:\nA) All advertisements about health products lack scientific basis.\nB) Nucleic acid in the human body will decrease with age.\nC) Illness is the result of malnutrition.\nD) Eating health products may not promote your health.', "<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and analyze each option step by step:\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**\n   - The context states that nucleic acids and other genetic foods in health care products are not very helpful to human health.\n   - It mentions that the claim of needing exogenous nucleic acids is scientifically unfounded.\n   - The context also states that the human body lacks nutrition, not nucleic acid.\n   - It further clarifies that the claim about weakened gene-making ability due to aging is false.\n\n2.**Option A: All advertisements about health products lack scientific basis.**\n   - The context does not explicitly state that all advertisements about health products lack scientific basis.It only mentions that specific claims about nucleic acids are not supported by science.\n   - Therefore, we cannot infer this option based on the given information.\n\n3.**Option B: Nucleic acid in the human body will decrease with age.**\n   - The context does not provide any information about the age-related changes in nucleic acid levels in the human body.\n   - It only mentions that the ability to make genes might be weakened, but this is not directly related to nucleic acid levels.\n   - Therefore, we cannot infer this option based on the given information.\n\n4.**Option C: Illness is the result of malnutrition.**\n   - The context does not explicitly state that illness is the result of malnutrition.\n   - It only mentions that the human body lacks nutrition, not that illness is directly caused by malnutrition.Eating health products may promote your health based on the given information.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
