messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn Berinia, the age at which people could begin to drink alcohol legally used to be 18. In 1990, in an attempt to reduce alcohol consumption and thereby to reduce alcohol-related traffic deaths among Berinians under 21, the legal drinking age was raised to 21. Alcohol-related traffic deaths among people under 21 have decreased significantly since 1990. Nevertheless, surveys show that people in that age-group drink just as much alcohol as they did before 1990.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true of Berinia, most helps to resolve the apparent discrepancy?\n# Options:\nA) Alcohol-related traffic deaths among people over 21 have increased slightly since 1990.\nB) For the population as a whole, annual alcohol consumption is no lower now than it was in 1990.\nC) The proportion of people under 21 who own a car is higher now than it was in 1990.\nD) Alcohol consumption away from home, for example in bars and restaurants, is much lower among people under 21 than it was in 1990.', "<think>.\nTo resolve the apparent discrepancy, we need to understand why alcohol-related traffic deaths have decreased despite the increase in alcohol consumption among people under 21.The context suggests that the legal drinking age was raised to 21, which likely led to fewer young people driving under the influence of alcohol.Let's analyze each option to see which one best explains this phenomenon:.\nA) Alcohol-related traffic deaths among people over 21 have increased slightly since 1990.\n- This option does not directly address the discrepancy between alcohol consumption and traffic deaths among young people.It does not mention a trend for people over 21, which is relevant to the question.\nB) For the population as a whole, annual alcohol consumption is lower now than it was in 1990.\n- This option suggests that overall alcohol consumption has decreased, which aligns with the context that alcohol-related traffic deaths have decreased. Therefore, it helps resolve the discrepancy.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
