messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the conclusion drawn from it.The context mentions that fraudulent text messages are still prevalent despite being exposed by the media, and that professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy messages rather than more deceptive ones.The conclusion drawn is that swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\nTo refute this conclusion, we need an option that directly challenges the idea that swindlers are stupid or unprofessional.Let's examine each option:.\n\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\n- This option directly contradicts the conclusion by stating that swindlers need to be smart to deceive others.If swindlers are smart, they are not necessarily stupid or unprofessional.This option strongly refutes the conclusion.\n\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\n- This option discusses the swindlers' strategy to avoid detection but does not address their intelligence or professionalism.It does not directly challenge the conclusion about their stupidity or unprofessionalism.\n\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\n- This option suggests that swindlers are efficient and would eliminate ineffective methods.Even though this suggests a certain degree of intelligence, it does not contradict the assertion regarding their lack of foolishness or amateurism.\n\nB) Fraudsters employ these messages to ensnare individuals who might be deceived, and they seek to exclude intelligent individuals initially.\n- This choice outlines the fraudsters' tactics without specifically mentioning their intelligence or professionalism. It does not dispute the assertion about their stupidity or unprofessionalism.\n\nUpon evaluating all the choices, the option that effectively supports the claim that swindlers are not excessively foolish and unprofessional is option B.\n</consider>.\n<response>\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
