messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWittgenstein was a student of Moore, a famous philosopher at Cambridge University. One day, philosopher Russell asked Moore, who is your best student? Moore said without hesitation: Wittgenstein. why? because among all the students, only he always showed a blank look when listening to the class, and there were always endless questions. later, Wittgenstein is more famous than Russell. Someone asked, why did Russell fall behind? Wittgenstein said: he has no problem.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, this paragraph is intended to illustrate that:\n# Options:\nA) Doubting and questioning are always the secret of success\nB) Curiosity is the internal driving force of research\nC) Appreciation is an important factor in success\nD) Finding problems is the premise of continuous progress', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's carefully analyze the context and the question.The context provides us with a scenario where Wittgenstein, a student of Moore, is praised for his unique behavior in class and his persistent questioning.Later, Wittgenstein attributes his success to his ability to find problems, which he claims Russell lacks.The question asks us to determine the main point the paragraph is trying to illustrate.\n\nFirst, let's examine each option:.\n\nA) Doubting and questioning are always the secret of success:.\n- This option asserts that curiosity is not the internal driving force of research. It emphasizes that questioning and doubting are not always beneficial for success, as evidenced by Wittgenstein's behavior and claim about Russell.\nHowever, the context does not mention any evidence supporting this assertion.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
