 94%|#########3| 564/600 [18:45<00:25,  1.44it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWith the further increase of global meat production, the impact of animal husbandry on Greenhouse Effect of the world will also increase. At present, animal husbandry land has accounted for 30% of the earth's land area. As one of the fastest growing sectors of agriculture, animal husbandry also takes up more land for feed and grazing. In Latin America, 70% of forests have been cut down to make room for pastures. At present, animal husbandry threatens 306 of the world's 825 terrestrial ecosystems and threatens 1699 endangered species.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is intended to be explained in this paragraph?\n# Options:\nA) The environmental cost of developing animal husbandry.\nB) The development of animal husbandry should be strictly controlled.\nC) Bottleneck in the development of animal husbandry.\nD) Serious pollution caused by animal husbandry.", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, I need to carefully analyze the context and question provided.The context discusses the increasing impact of animal husbandry on the environment, particularly the land use and ecosystem disruption caused by it.The question asks which option best explains the information given in the context.Let's evaluate each option step by step:.\n\nA) The environmental cost of developing animal husbandry.\n- This option aligns well with the context.The paragraph mentions that animal husbandry is taking up more land for feed and grazing, leading to deforestation and threatening ecosystems.This directly addresses the environmental costs associated with animal husbandry development.\n\nB) The development of animal husbandry should be strictly controlled.\n- While this option could be inferred from the context, it is 