100%|#########9| 597/600 [19:04<00:01,  1.83it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAntagonism is a common sensory change phenomenon, which refers to the phenomenon that the presence of one odorous substance weakens the taste characteristics of another odorant.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings does not exhibit antagonism?\n# Options:\nA) Adding a small amount of citric acid to orange juice will reduce the sweetness, and adding sugar will reduce the sour taste\nB) Saccharin has a bitter taste. adding a small amount of sodium glutamate to saccharin can significantly alleviate the bitter taste\nC) After taking sodium chloride and quinine at the same time, drinking water will have a slightly sweet feeling\nD) After eating sour sambal, and then eating sour food, you will not taste the sour taste', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to understand the concept of antagonism as defined in the context.Antagonism refers to the phenomenon where the presence of one odorant weakens the taste characteristics of another odorant.This means that when two substances are present together, the overall effect on taste is less than the sum of their individual effects.\n\nLet's analyze each option to determine if it exhibits antagonism:.\n\nA) Adding a small amount of citric acid to orange juice will reduce the sweetness, and adding sugar will reduce the sour taste.\n- This option describes a situation where the presence of citric acid (one substance) reduces the sweetness (taste characteristic) of orange juice, and the presence of sugar (another substance) reduces the sour taste.This fits the definition of antagonism because the presence of one substance weakens the taste characteristic of another substance.\n\nB) Saccharin has a bitter taste.Adding a small amount of sodium glutamate to saccharin can significantly alleviate the bitter taste.\nAfter consuming sour sambal, and subsequently consuming other sour foods, you will still perceive the sour taste. This situation aligns with the concept of taste enhancement, as the sourness of the foods intensifies rather than diminishes.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
